# Post-Commit Review

Mandatory after **every successful `git commit` agent runs** — before ending turn or reporting done.

## 1. Simplify

Skip unless `git show --shortstat --format='' HEAD` insertions + deletions **> 100**.

If over threshold, follow `.cursor/skills/simplify/SKILL.md` on commit just made:

- **Scope:** `git show --stat --patch --no-color HEAD`
- Main thread: parallel read-only reviewers → targeted inline fixes
- Stage simplify fixes; **do not commit** unless user already asked for commit this turn

## 2. Launch review subagent

One `bugbot` subagent (`run_in_background: false`):

```text
Full Repository Path: <workspace root>
Diff: natural language
Change Description: <output of `git show --stat HEAD` plus `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD`; if §1 produced staged fixes, also include `git diff --cached --no-color`>
Custom Instructions: Follow `.cursor/skills/caveman-review/SKILL.md`. Output only findings in `path:line: <emoji> <severity>: <problem>. <fix>.` format. End with `totals: N🔴 N🟡 N🔵 N❓` or `No issues.`
```

If diff unavailable, retry once with file contents from `git show HEAD --name-only`.

## 3. Apply findings

| Severity | Emoji | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|
| High | 🔴 `bug:` | Fix inline before ending turn |
| Medium | 🟡 `risk:` | Fix inline before ending turn |
| Low | 🔵 `nit:` | Skip |
| Question | ❓ `q:` | Skip |

Apply code-level fixes inline (main thread). Keep each fix minimal. Findings needing product/architecture call: skip fix, report to user — they do **not** block ending turn.

## 4. After fixes

If any 🔴/🟡 fixed inline:

1. Lint touched files
2. Stage fixes; **do not commit** unless user already asked for commit this turn
3. Report staged fixes and offer commit; user decides

## 5. Report

One line: simplify summary (if any), review findings count, what was fixed, what was skipped (nits, questions, ambiguous).

## Exclusions

- Commit failed or was aborted → skip
- User says "commit only" / "no review" → skip review + simplify
